WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.692
You followed Learn's procedure,
saw where its outputs fall short,

3
00:00:04.692 --> 00:00:07.716
and met the build that makes
the same MOF every time,

4
00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:12.613
checks the package and the definition, and
refuses what the registry doesn't allow.

5
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:14.373
The evidence an ISSO keeps:

6
00:00:14.373 --> 00:00:18.773
both provenance files and the
findings file in the evidence store,

7
00:00:18.773 --> 00:00:23.493
the registry and its pull requests, and
in Lab 2, the published blob's hash,

8
00:00:23.493 --> 00:00:27.253
the role assignment, the
definition's activity log entry,

9
00:00:27.253 --> 00:00:31.013
and each machine's compliance
against the recorded hash.

10
00:00:31.013 --> 00:00:34.762
Before shipping, work through
the Chapter 07 checklist.

11
00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:39.276
Next is Module 6: onboard
servers with Ansible beside Arc.

12
00:00:39.276 --> 00:00:43.009
You'll read a CMDB export into
groups and tags, plan a wave,

13
00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:47.380
and see what each server would
get before anything is contacted.
